  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Determination\\n\\n**Neither record applies as written.** This workspace does not have a single \\\"observation cursor\\\" whose behaviour is either global (Record A) or per-consumer (Record B). The behaviour it actually implements and ships is a **two-cursor contract** — `EventCursor ≠ ViewCursor` — so the two records are each describing one half of the real contract while claiming to be the whole of it.\\n\\nIf the question is narrowed to the *observation* cursor proper (the token a consumer holds and sends back to observe staleness), the applicable behaviour is **per-consumer (Record B's shape)**. The global \\\"one position shared by all readers\\\" behaviour (Record A's shape) belongs to the **canonical event cursor**, which the spec explicitly declares to be a *different* thing.\\n\\n## Why this is the decision\\n\\n**1. Both `09-observation-contract-*.md` files fail the repo's own authority test.**\\n\\n- The engineering archive is registered in `docs/engineering/README.md`. Slot `09` is already occupied there by `09-adaptive-allocation-spec.md` (PLMP-ALC-1). Neither `09-observation-contract-a.md` nor `-b.md` is listed in the index — they are unregistered files colliding on an occupied slo",
